Marks the position that the WebGPU fill extrusion vertex shaders output as
@invariant, as the Metal shaders mark theirs [[invariant]]. A translucent or
patterned extrusion draws twice: a depth-only pass, then a color pass that
passes the depth test only where its depth is less than or equal to the depth
the first pass wrote. The passes use different pipelines, and without
invariance a shader compiler may compute the position differently in each, so
the color pass fails in scattered blocks and stripes and buildings show holes.
Chrome on macOS showed this. Chrome on Linux with Vulkan didn't.
Upstream: https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-native/pull/4939

diff --git a/include/mln/shaders/webgpu/fill_extrusion.hpp b/include/mln/shaders/webgpu/fill_extrusion.hpp
index 79ffe8a..1fb670d 100644
--- a/include/mln/shaders/webgpu/fill_extrusion.hpp
+++ b/include/mln/shaders/webgpu/fill_extrusion.hpp
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@ struct VertexInput {
 };
 
 struct VertexOutput {
-    @builtin(position) position: vec4<f32>,
+    @builtin(position) @invariant position: vec4<f32>,
     @location(0) color: vec4<f32>,
 };
 
@@ -172,7 +172,7 @@ struct VertexInput {
 };
 
 struct VertexOutput {
-    @builtin(position) position: vec4<f32>,
+    @builtin(position) @invariant position: vec4<f32>,
     @location(0) lighting: vec4<f32>,
     @location(1) pos_a: vec2<f32>,
     @location(2) pos_b: vec2<f32>,
